+    The map is authored in Notion and reaches this check as either a Markdown pipe
+    table or an HTML table; the destination is written as a bare URL or as a
+    `<mention-page url="...">` element.  An earlier version accepted only the pipe
+    table with a bare URL, so it matched nothing against the real body and reported
+    a class-map defect on a correct map -- information about the check, not the body,
+    which is the same failure `notion_page_identity` was introduced to end.  Both
+    renderings are accepted here; the third element is the raw destination field and
+    identity is resolved by the caller, never compared as text.
+    """
